  app/static/vendor/d3/LICENSE
- Swagger UI 5.33.1 (Apache-2.0), https://swagger.io/tools/swagger-ui/
  app/static/vendor/swagger-ui/LICENSE and NOTICE
  (Copyright 2020-2021 SmartBear Software Inc.)
- ReDoc 2.5.4 (MIT), https://redocly.com/redoc
  app/static/vendor/redoc/LICENSE; the packages bundled into it are listed in
  app/static/vendor/redoc/redoc.standalone.js.LICENSE.txt

docker/mtdna-server-2/report.Rmd and docker/mtdna-server-2/files/
rcrs_mutserve.fasta are copied unchanged from mtDNA-Server 2 v2.1.16
(https://github.com/genepi/mtdna-server-2: reports/report.Rmd and
files/rcrs_mutserve.fasta), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 Hansi
Weißensteiner; the licence text is in
docker/mtdna-server-2/LICENSE.mtdna-server-2. The FASTA is the revised
Cambridge Reference Sequence (NC_012920.1).

test_data/ holds PharmCAT's example VCFs and the reports PharmCAT produced from
them (https://github.com/PharmGKB/PharmCAT, MPL-2.0). The guidance text in those
reports is ClinPGx content (CC BY-SA 4.0, below).

app/static/demo/NA12878.pgx-demo.cram is cut from the 1000 Genomes Project's 30x
whole genome of NA12878 (run ERR3239334; Byrska-Bishop et al., Cell 2022,
doi:10.1016/j.cell.2022.08.004). The NA12878 cell line and DNA were obtained from
the NIGMS Human Genetic Cell Repository at the Coriell Institute for Medical
Research. These data were generated at the New York Genome Center with funds
provided by NHGRI Grant 3UM1HG008901-03S1.

lexicon/allele-table.csv, gene-table.csv and phenotype-table.csv are PyPGx
0.27.0's tables (https://github.com/sbslee/pypgx, pypgx/api/data/) without
their MT-RNR1 rows (24 allele rows, 1 gene row and 3 phenotype rows); apart
from line endings, nothing else in them is changed. MIT License, Copyright (c)
2020 Seung-been "Steven" Lee; the licence text is in lexicon/LICENSE.pypgx.
lexicon/phenotypes.tsv lists PharmCAT's alleles and phenotypes, which are CPIC
and ClinPGx content (below).

app/genome/grch38_contig_names.tsv maps GRCh38's RefSeq and GenBank accessions
to UCSC names and lengths. scripts/make_grch38_contig_names.py writes it from
NCBI's GRCh38 assembly reports (GCF_000001405.26 and GCF_000001405.40); NCBI
places no restrictions on their use.

docker/fhir-server/packages/ holds three FHIR packages, unmodified, from HL7's
FHIR package registry (https://packages.fhir.org), which the bundled HAPI FHIR
server loads: the Genomics Reporting Implementation Guide 3.0.0, HL7
Terminology (THO) 6.1.0 and the FHIR Extensions Pack 5.1.0. HL7 publishes
them under CC0 1.0. Some of their value sets list LOINC and SNOMED CT codes,
which come with those terminologies' terms (section 4).


