3. Data the stack downloads or carries, and its terms
-----------------------------------------------------

- ClinPGx (formerly PharmGKB), carried by PharmCAT: allele definitions, guideline
  and drug-label annotations. Used under the Creative Commons Attribution-
  ShareAlike 4.0 International License
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/); ClinPGx's terms ask that
  the data be used for research purposes and not offered for sale.
  https://www.clinpgx.org/page/dataUsagePolicy
- CPIC guidelines, through ClinPGx: CC0 1.0. CPIC asks for attribution and notes
  that its guidelines change; refer to https://www.clinpgx.org/cpic for the
  current ones. CPIC® is a registered service mark of the U.S. Department of
  Health & Human Services (HHS).
- PharmVar star-allele definitions, through CPIC and ClinPGx: CC BY-SA 4.0, for
  research use. https://www.pharmvar.org/terms-and-conditions
- DPWG guidelines (KNMP), through ClinPGx. FDA tables: U.S. Government work.
- PharmCAT's GRCh38 reference FASTA: Woon M, Zenodo,
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.7288118, CC BY 4.0; derived from NCBI's GRCh38 analysis set.
- PharmCAT's position list (pharmcat_positions_3.4.0.vcf, from its v3.4.0
  release) and regions BED (pharmcat_regions.bed, from its development branch),
  which the genome downloader fetches from GitHub: MPL-2.0,
  https://github.com/PharmGKB/PharmCAT.
- UCSC hg38 and hg19 FASTAs: freely available; UCSC asks that data be credited.
  The hg19ToHg38 liftover chain: "The UCSC Chain Files are property of The
  Regents of the University of California, and made available free for
  non-commercial use by Independent Researchers and Nonprofit Organizations.
  Any other use of UCSC Chain Files requires a commercial license". The genome
  downloader fetches it from UCSC; downloading it accepts UCSC's End User
  License Agreement, https://genome.ucsc.edu/license/EULA.pdf.
- 1000 Genomes Project data: the GRCh37 reference human_g1k_v37 and the GRCh38
  full analysis set with decoys and HLA
  (GRCh38_full_analysis_set_plus_decoy_hla.fa, for the CRAM reference cache),
  which the genome downloader fetches from the 1000 Genomes FTP site
  (https://ftp.1000genomes.ebi.ac.uk); the phasing panels inside PyPGx's
  resource bundle; and the NA12878 reads in the demo CRAM (section 1).
  EMBL-EBI terms of use, Fort Lauderdale principles. The 30x data were
  generated at the New York Genome Center with funds provided by NHGRI Grants
  3UM1HG008901-03S1 and 3UM1HG008901-04S2, from cell lines and DNA samples
  obtained from the NIGMS Human Genetic Cell Repository at the Coriell
  Institute for Medical Research.
- IPD-IMGT/HLA sequences, in OptiType's reference: Creative Commons
  Attribution-NoDerivs. https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ipd/imgt/hla/licence/
- PhyloTree 17 (van Oven and Kayser) and its Forensic Update (Dür, Huber and
  Parson), in Haplogrep 3's tree.
- dbSNP and GRCh38: NCBI places no restrictions on their use.


